/* Wong Tai Sin Oracle Sticks data (English) · Source and variant records: docs/qian-data-sources/huangdaxian.md */
window.QIAN_DATA = {
  id: "huangdaxian",
  total: 100,
  name: "Wong Tai Sin Oracle Sticks",
  nameZh: "黄大仙灵签",
  grades: ["上上", "上吉", "中吉", "中平", "下下"],
  gradeLabels: { "上上": "Supremely Auspicious", "上吉": "Very Auspicious", "中吉": "Auspicious", "中平": "Neutral", "下下": "Very Inauspicious" },
  aspects: ["Marriage", "Career", "Wealth", "Health"],
  signs: [
    { no: 1, grade: "上上", title: "Jiang Taigong Made Prime Minister", titleZh: "姜公封相", poem: "You draw the very first stick of the lot\nAs dragon meets tiger where wind and cloud converge\nOne day soaring past the highest heavens\nFree to come and go at the Jade Pool", poemZh: "灵签求得第一枝\n龙虎风云际会时\n一旦凌霄扬自乐\n任君来往赴瑶池", meaning: "This stick recalls Jiang Taigong, met by King Wen while fishing at the Wei River and raised to prime minister - dragon and tiger joined by wind and cloud. The finest of the hundred: what you seek ripens when the moment arrives, with patrons converging. Career and wealth, main and side income, all flourish; marriage and household prosper. Seize the hour boldly, stay humble, and the fortune climbs higher still.", aspects: ["Destined match", "Patrons help", "All wealth thrives", "Sound health"] },
    { no: 2, grade: "上吉", title: "Wang Daozhen Stumbles Into the Peach Blossom Spring", titleZh: "王道真误入桃源", poem: "Withered trees put forth new buds at spring's return\nFragrant blooms and lush leaves draw butterflies in swarms\nA thousand reds and purples vie in the Peach Blossom Spring\nA lone fishing boat strays into its hidden ford", poemZh: "枯木逢春尽发新\n花香叶茂蝶来频\n桃源竞斗千红紫\n一叶渔舟误入津", meaning: "Wang Daozhen's boat strays into the hidden Peach Blossom Spring, where withered trees bud anew and butterflies throng among fragrant blooms - misfortune turning sweet. The best scenes come unsought: career flows into place, a destined partner may appear, and unexpected money arrives. Act with the season and enjoy your blessings, yet curb speculation and restless craving, so the good spell endures.", aspects: ["Meet your match", "Effortless success", "Unexpected gains", "Refreshed and well"] },
    { no: 3, grade: "中平", title: "Lu Ban and the Mountain Trees", titleZh: "鲁班开山", poem: "The timber of Mount Niu was fine and fair\nYet the woodman's axe felled it all away\nGreat beams and worthy wood left none to use\nHow can a circle be drawn with a faulty compass", poemZh: "牛山之木皆常美\n独惜斧工尽伐他\n大器大材无足用\n规矩不准怎为搓", meaning: "Lu Ban's axes fell every fine tree on Mount Niu, until even the greatest timber has no use at all. You hold good material now, but careless handling or trusting the wrong people can squander it. In career, defend rather than attack; refuse windfalls and easy money. Move step by step, follow the rules, and treasure the resources in hand to keep your foundation.", aspects: ["Not yet time", "Defend, don't attack", "Guard your money", "Minor ailments"] },
    { no: 4, grade: "中吉", title: "Dong Yong Meets a Fairy", titleZh: "董永遇仙", poem: "Purple swallows feed their young beneath the eaves\nWarbling softly through the noontide air\nThey dart and swoop, now low, now rising\nAt times their wings slice the green willow haze", poemZh: "调雏紫燕在檐前\n对语呢喃近午天\n或往或来低复起\n有时剪破绿杨烟", meaning: "Dong Yong's filial devotion moved a fairy to descend and marry him; swallows feed their young beneath the eaves in a picture of gentle contentment. Fortune is steady with small rises and dips, like swallows dipping and soaring. Marriage luck is good and a wedding can succeed; work and money bring modest, reliable gains. Stay humble and diligent, and things gradually improve.", aspects: ["Wedding succeeds", "Steady progress", "Modest gains", "Mind your rest"] },
    { no: 5, grade: "中吉", title: "Lady Han Cherishes the Flowers", titleZh: "韩夫人惜花", poem: "A fierce storm swept the east garden last night\nToppling every blossom, purple and red\nLuckily the flower-lover rose at dawn\nTo firm the roots and plant them back to life", poemZh: "东园昨夜狂风急\n万紫千红亦尽倾\n幸有惜花人早起\n培回根本复栽生", meaning: "After the gale flattens every flower in the east garden, the early-rising flower lover props the roots and replants them, and life returns. A turbulent year lies ahead; timing and place are against you, so lean on people and patrons to pull through. Expect modest money, guard romance from setbacks, and prepare early. Heaven helps those who help themselves, and growth will return.", aspects: ["Weather the storm", "Hold and wait", "Curb ambition", "Treat early"] },
    { no: 6, grade: "上吉", title: "Wang Xizhi Returns to His Native Place", titleZh: "王羲之归故里", poem: "A lone sail returns from ten thousand miles\nSet down the cup, let pipes and strings play on\nClouds of fine friends chat of wind and moon\nPouring out their hearts in pure delight", poemZh: "一片孤帆万里回\n管弦呕哑且停杯\n如云胜友谈风月\n畅叙幽情极乐哉", meaning: "Wang Xizhi, the Sage of Calligraphy, resigns office and sails ten thousand miles home to talk of wind and moon with friends - success crowned by ease. A largely fortunate year: fame and profit together, strongest in autumn and winter; household thriving, love harmonious. Settle into the good days, share your joy through good deeds, and the run of luck stretches long.", aspects: ["Harmonious union", "Fame and profit", "All channels fine", "Safe and healthy"] },
    { no: 7, grade: "中吉", title: "Xue Rengui Returns Home", titleZh: "仁贵归家", poem: "Autumn wild geese wing their way to the south\nRed leaves whirl and scatter through the courtyard\nThe sound of fulling blocks chills the ear on the ramparts\nRiver maples blaze like fire by the fishing shore", poemZh: "秋来征雁向南归\n红叶纷纷满院飞\n砧捣城头声切耳\n江枫如火在渔矶", meaning: "Xue Rengui returns from victory in the east, honored and homeward bound - yet autumn geese and falling leaves shade the joy with bleakness. Spring and summer serve you better; from autumn on, double your care. Achievement is real but expansion tempts fate, money stays level and theft threatens, and romance may spark friction - no need to rush a wedding. Know sufficiency and quit while ahead.", aspects: ["Defuse quarrels", "Steady success", "Keep level", "Care after autumn"] },
    { no: 8, grade: "下下", title: "The Dove Seizes the Magpie's Nest", titleZh: "鸠占鹊巢", poem: "The cooing dove seizes the magpie's nest\nGuest and host sit ill at ease together\nTall pines line the ridge with vines entwined\nPonder what riddle these verses hold", poemZh: "鸣鸠争夺鹊巢居\n宾主参差意不舒\n满岭乔松萝茑附\n且猜诗语是何如", meaning: "The dove seizes the magpie's nest and creeping vines entangle the pines: a year of petty intruders and uneasy alliances. Disputes multiply; in business beware others taking what you built, and holding your ground already counts as gain. Speak little, move carefully, shun greed and quarrels, and never wrestle the strong head-on. Do good, yield graciously, and wait for the season to turn.", aspects: ["Beware intruders", "Defend your ground", "Hold the line", "Guard against illness"] },
    { no: 9, grade: "上吉", title: "Tao Yuanming Admires Chrysanthemums", titleZh: "陶渊明赏菊", poem: "A new tune rises from the jade zither\nBright moon and cool breeze chill the pillow mat\nHonored guests all gather to admire the chrysanthemums\nSome sing, some dance, some pass the winecup around", poemZh: "瑶琴一曲奏新腔\n明月清风枕簟凉\n咸集嘉宾同赏菊\n或歌或舞或飞觞", meaning: "Tao Yuanming, resigning office, admires chrysanthemums by the eastern hedge amid music, moonlight and gathered guests - season, place and people all favorable. Things go smoothly, with luck rising after the start of autumn; married couples grow closer, singles can find their match, and the household may welcome a child. Take contentment as it comes; fame and profit arrive unbidden when the time is right.", aspects: ["Fine match awaits", "Smooth and pleasing", "Money comes naturally", "Well in season"] },
    { no: 10, grade: "中平", title: "Su Qin Fails the Exams", titleZh: "苏秦不第", poem: "A mirror moon hangs high in the sky\nYet drifting clouds veil it fold on fold\nWhen will the jade case flash forth its light\nWho will lend me a mighty gust of wind", poemZh: "一轮月镜挂空中\n偶被浮云障叠重\n玉匣何时光气吐\n谁人借我一狂风", meaning: "Su Qin failed the exams repeatedly before wearing the seals of six states; a bright moon now hangs veiled beneath layer upon layer of drifting cloud. Your hour has not struck: plans stall at the last step for want of a patron to lend the wind. Hold your temper, prepare quietly, and strengthen yourself while you wait; when the wind shifts, the light will show.", aspects: ["Wait for timing", "Hold and prepare", "Wealth delayed", "Patient recovery"] },
    { no: 11, grade: "上吉", title: "Emperor Wen of Han Admires the Willows", titleZh: "汉文帝赏柳", poem: "Willows drape the banks and lock in green mist\nLong days stir them to wake and drowse again\nPurple swallows flutter to and fro\nGraceful in the wind, so lovely to behold", poemZh: "杨柳垂堤锁绿烟\n日长三起又三眠\n往来紫燕纷飞舞\n袅娜迎风倩我怜", meaning: "Emperor Wen strolls among bank-side willows while swallows dance - a reign of gentle virtue and a people at ease, promising fulfillment on all fronts. A lucky year: career advances toward promotion, steady income rolls in, marriage proves a match made in heaven, and the household prospers. Do the work yourself, store up merit, and use the spring-summer window to let momentum swell.", aspects: ["Blessed match", "Promotion coming", "Ample salary", "Few illnesses"] },
    { no: 12, grade: "下下", title: "Li Bai Grasps at the Moon", titleZh: "太白捞月", poem: "Mirage towers rise beyond all bounds\nTen thousand feet of them propping up the sky\nA wild gust may scatter them in a breath\nThen they re-gather, coiling like blue smoke", poemZh: "蜃楼海市幻无边\n万丈擎空接上天\n或被狂风忽吹散\n有时仍聚结青烟", meaning: "Li Bai, drunk, reaches for the moon's reflection; the splendid towers are mirages that a gust disperses like smoke. The prosperity before your eyes may be illusion: schemes risk coming up empty, money eludes capture, and fame cannot be forced. Beware flattery and glittering bait. Stand on solid ground, do good quietly, refuse sweet-talking shortcuts, and protect your foundations above all.", aspects: ["Illusory romance", "No rash moves", "Wealth may vanish", "Prevention first"] },
    { no: 13, grade: "中平", title: "Meng Haoran Seeks Plum Blossoms", titleZh: "孟浩然寻梅", poem: "A single plum branch blooms first south of the ranges\nIts petals, crystal bright, drift into the winecup\nBut one on a donkey arrived earlier still\nA child bears off the crown of spring", poemZh: "岭南初放一枝梅\n片片晶莹入酒杯\n却遇骑驴人早至\n儿童背负占春魁", meaning: "Meng Haoran rides off in search of plum blossoms, only to find the donkey rider ahead has claimed the first branch of spring. Your late-winter and early-spring outlook is best; schemes bring no triumph but no disaster either. Money stays flat, partners may claim a share, and romance can tangle. Move first - one step quicker than the rest - and the crown of spring can be yours.", aspects: ["May be preempted", "Move first", "Modest, no greed", "Stronger in spring"] },
    { no: 14, grade: "中吉", title: "Su Dongpo Drunk Among Flowers", titleZh: "苏东坡醉酒", poem: "For love of quiet leisure, plant more bamboo\nBuy spring, enjoy the rain, in a thatched hut\nDrunk, lie down beside the apricot blossoms\nOnly fear the oriole's cry disturbing deep dreams", poemZh: "为爱幽闲多种竹\n买春赏雨在茅屋\n醉时卧倒杏花边\n怕听莺儿惊梦熟", meaning: "Su Dongpo plants bamboo, savors rain in a thatched hut, and sleeps drunk among apricot blossoms - ease and contentment rather than grandeur. The year is not perfect, but remarkably carefree: work pleasant, livelihood ample, no windfalls and no need to chase unwed love. One warning hides inside the ease - guard your tongue against gossip and dispute; keep your mouth shut and the calm holds.", aspects: ["Love not yet", "Content at work", "Ample livelihood", "Rest and restore"] },
    { no: 15, grade: "上吉", title: "Emperor Minghuang Visits the Moon Palace", titleZh: "明皇游月殿", poem: "An immortal raft drifts down the midstream\nRoam at will through the palace of the moon\nThe Rainbow Skirt song fills your ears, then pauses\nWith wine and verse, when will the revels end", poemZh: "仙槎一叶泛中流\n月殿蟾宫任尔游\n盈耳霓裳声暂歇\n酒诗吟饮几时休", meaning: "Emperor Minghuang sails a leaf of an immortal raft to the moon palace and learns the Rainbow Skirt melody - a reign at peace, a season of feasting. A greatly fortunate year: career delivers fame and profit, income flows from main and side channels, and engagement or marriage is perfectly timed. Yet the poem whispers a caution - do not drown in pleasure; moderation in success keeps the splendor alive.", aspects: ["Marry in joy", "Fame and profit", "Both channels flow", "Illness soon healed"] },
    { no: 16, grade: "中吉", title: "Liu Bei Meets Master Shuijing", titleZh: "皇叔遇水镜", poem: "Crows wing back at sunset's edge of sky\nBeyond the ridges children ride their calves home\nThe Qiang flute sounds again, piercing the ear\nLong notes and short, what joy they bring", poemZh: "天边鸦背夕阳回\n陇外儿童跨犊来\n羌笛频吹声切耳\n短长腔调乐何哉", meaning: "Liu Bei chances upon Master Shuijing as crows return at dusk and herd boys ride home piping on Qiang flutes - an unhurried pastoral calm. Do your honest best and let results settle as they will: this is late-blooming greatness. The year holds no storms; sustained effort yields a year-end harvest. Love approaches but early marriage is unwise. Do your part, accept heaven's part, and enjoy the work.", aspects: ["Timing approaches", "Late bloomer", "Save steadily", "Safe and sound"] },
    { no: 17, grade: "中吉", title: "Pursuing a Sage by Moonlight", titleZh: "月下追贤", poem: "Autumn waters, white dew heavy on the reeds\nCourtyard moonlight steeps the steps in clarity\nA fresh breeze sets the horse bells ringing\nTheir chime runs on to meet the morning bell", poemZh: "秋水蒹葭白露盈\n盈庭月色浸阶清\n清风吹动马铃响\n响接晨钟不断声", meaning: "Xiao He chases Han Xin by moonlight; what was lost returns, talent finds its use, and each line rings into the next like unbroken horse bells - help arriving in relay. An ordinary start gives way, after autumn, to a patron who values you; consider a bold career move. Main income stays modest while side income shines. Love is timely - guard against small jealous flare-ups.", aspects: ["Good timing", "Patron's favor", "Side income shines", "No serious illness"] },
    { no: 18, grade: "下下", title: "The Cuckoo's Blood-Stained Cry", titleZh: "杜鹃泣血动客心", poem: "The cuckoo cries blood, its voice all sorrow\nThe bitter sound startles dreams in frosty cold\nIt stirs the stranger lodged in a strange land\nAnd the wanderer's heart turns to his home garden", poemZh: "杜鹃啼血泪悲声\n声怨霜寒梦乍惊\n惊动异乡为异客\n客心更触故园情", meaning: "The cuckoo weeps blood and the wanderer's heart aches in a strange land - a bleak, unsettled picture of repeated setbacks. Schemes struggle this year; money comes hard and side income is out of the question - gambling especially forbidden. Quarrels strain romance and separation threatens the household. Speak little, do much, and steer carefully through spring and autumn; even so, hardship can soften toward fortune.", aspects: ["Not for marrying", "Stay employed", "No gambling", "Guard heart, lungs"] },
    { no: 19, grade: "中吉", title: "Fuxi Draws the Eight Trigrams", titleZh: "伏羲画八卦", poem: "Qian, three lines whole, bears the sign of the sun\nThe submerged dragon, still unused, heads the first chapter\nPenetrate the meaning of the lines within\nAnd a hundred blessings arrive in radiant accord", poemZh: "乾卦三连号太阳\n潜龙勿用第一章\n其中爻象能参透\n百福骈臻大吉昌", meaning: "Fuxi draws the eight trigrams: Qian, all yang, yet its opening line counsels 'the submerged dragon does not yet act.' Hide your light, gather strength, and bide your time. Each season of the year carries good luck; a slow start in career is offset by endurance, and wealth turns from bitter to sweet with the later years best. Read every side, drop stubbornness, and blessings will come.", aspects: ["Think thrice", "Build momentum", "Bitter then sweet", "Avoid fiery foods"] },
    { no: 20, grade: "中平", title: "Xuemei Seeks a Husband with a Couplet", titleZh: "雪梅招亲", poem: "Immortal flowers in heaven, no asking their seed\nMortal affairs below shift how many times\nThe road ahead is written in ledgers public and private\nPunishment and reward divide the muddy from the clear", poemZh: "天上仙花难问种\n人间尘事几多更\n前程已注公私簿\n罚赏分明浊与清", meaning: "Xuemei sets a couplet challenge to find a husband, and the worthy answer wins her hand - a heaven-granted match with clear accounts. The road ahead is inscribed in the ledgers of fate: good deeds make wishes attainable, while wealth is allotted, not seized. The year improves toward its close; steady cultivation earns its harvest. Honor your spouse like a guest - harmony at home is what draws prosperity in.", aspects: ["Heaven-sent match", "Work earns harvest", "Cannot be forced", "Choose doctors wisely"] },
    { no: 21, grade: "中吉", title: "Empress Wu Zetian Admires the Flowers", titleZh: "武则天赏花", poem: "Crimson clouds beyond the sky spread like brocade\nPeach and apricot by the railing vie in new dress\nA dazzle fills the eyes - who ranks first\nPour the fine wine freely, but drink with measure", poemZh: "天外红霞如抹锦\n槛边桃杏斗新装\n盈眸烟熳谁居首\n美酒频斟且酌量", meaning: "Empress Wu drums the flowers into bloom and judges peach against apricot - pageantry, wealth, and pleasant stir. After the spring equinox a fine stretch opens, and the year holds far more good than harm; career yields unexpected gains, with money strongest through spring, summer, and winter. Amid the contest of blossoms the poem's last words counsel measure: avoid turning clever haste into blunder, and weigh each step.", aspects: ["Spring engagement", "Seize the moment", "No rash greed", "Rest enough"] },
    { no: 22, grade: "下下", title: "Chen Miaochang Longs for Love", titleZh: "陈妙常思春", poem: "Autumn waters keep two hearts a world apart\nBetween south sky and north earth the sorrow stretches long\nThis longing - tell me, who will carry it\nEndless desolation breaks the heart to madness", poemZh: "秋水依人各一方\n天南地北恨偏长\n相思试问凭谁寄\n不尽凄凉狂断肠", meaning: "The nun Chen Miaochang, stirred by human longing, misses her old companion across unbridgeable distance - a picture of chill solitude. Plans stall because resolve wavers: grasping and fretting, deciding and undoing, nothing gets done. Romance bears separation; marriage is unwise now; money is scarce and loss a real risk. Do good, pour yourself into one thing, and let a patron pull you through.", aspects: ["Separation looms", "One task only", "Guard against loss", "Keep spirits up"] },
    { no: 23, grade: "中平", title: "The Handan Dream", titleZh: "邯郸幻梦", poem: "The Handan dream sprawls without a border\nDecades of glory pass while millet still cooks\nIn brocade robes you return to your native place\nWaking, the whole of it lingers in the heart", poemZh: "邯郸一梦幻无边\n数载身荣是熟眠\n换却锦衣归故里\n睡醒还记在心田", meaning: "Scholar Lu dreams decades of rank and riches at an inn in Handan while the millet still steams - splendor that dissolves at waking. A year of appearance without substance: do not launch ventures, treat windfall money as a passing flower, and expect no wedding; guard against outside temptation and honeyed words. Drop the daydreams, keep your feet on the ground and your duty, and plain days go safely by.", aspects: ["No wedding yet", "Hold steady", "Bloom passes fast", "Steady the nerves"] },
    { no: 24, grade: "下下", title: "Bai Juyi Drinks Alone", titleZh: "白居易叹情", poem: "Poems, wine, qin and chess may soothe the sorrow\nBut with no guest in the seat the joy cannot last\nYou play, you sing - who truly knows its beauty\nCold cups aplenty, and still it turns to gloom", poemZh: "诗酒琴棋可解愁\n座中无客乐难休\n或弹或唱谁知美\n冷饮虽多亦是忧", meaning: "Bai Juyi, exiled to Jiangzhou, drinks alone: poetry and music pass the hours but cannot fill the empty seat. A soulmate is missing and lone effort stalls - the greater the hope, the deeper the disappointment. Blockages gather this year, with autumn the most delicate. Break out of self-imposed walls, widen your circle, and let good deeds lift the gloom; sinking spirits only drag fortune lower.", aspects: ["Soulmate scarce", "Don't force it", "Drop the fantasy", "Autumn illness alert"] },
    { no: 25, grade: "上吉", title: "Zhu Yuanzhang Ascends the Throne", titleZh: "朱洪武登基", poem: "Crowded mountains pay homage to the central peak\nLike ranked ministers in swan-file rows\nTwo lines stand arched in perfect order\nDwelling in this place, how could joy be absent", poemZh: "群山扰扰朝中岳\n有似为臣列鹄班\n拱立两行齐整肃\n自居此地岂无欢", meaning: "Zhu Yuanzhang takes the throne and the mountains bow to the sacred peak - high station, wide command, wishes made real. A very lucky year: long-held hopes come within reach, career climbs another story, and money channels open on every side. Marriage is favored, a child may be added to the house, and relocation anywhere opens a road. Ride the momentum and gather good-will; achievement rises with the tide.", aspects: ["Match made above", "Rising steadily", "Channels open", "Doctors cure fast"] },
    { no: 26, grade: "中平", title: "Xu Shu Hurries Home", titleZh: "徐庶归家", poem: "Flower shadows creep slowly up the steps\nFar off, a mirror moon hangs in the vast sky\nSuddenly the crane's cry, bleak and piercing\nBuy the homebound boat without delay", poemZh: "花影迟迟侵砌上\n遥知月镜挂长空\n忽闻鹤唳声凄切\n早买归舟返里中", meaning: "Xu Shu, heart pounding for his mother, commends Zhuge Liang and gallops away - the crane's cry calls the traveler home. Your heart is tied elsewhere and staying or leaving pulls both ways: the year's first half runs well, the second slides. Postpone romance to next year; watch elders' health in the household. Man proposes, heaven disposes - read the moment, then move, and knowing when keeps you safe.", aspects: ["Postpone for now", "Know the hour", "Take, don't crave", "Watch elders' health"] },
    { no: 27, grade: "中平", title: "Butterflies and Ants Know Their Season", titleZh: "蝶蚁知时", poem: "Under clearing skies powdered butterflies sun their wings\nBefore the courtyard the ant columns form\nRank on rank, advancing or withdrawing in order\nNow opening, now closing - how fine their timing", poemZh: "天晴粉蝶翻衣晒\n又看庭前蚁阵排\n队伍整齐趋或退\n时开时合思何佳", meaning: "Butterflies spread their wings in sunshine; ants advance and close ranks by season - even tiny creatures read the hour and follow it. A steady year: plans succeed by timing, money stays thin and cannot be forced, while romance favors you and home is calm. After winter, mind petty people; let earnings come from labor, not luck. Like the ant columns, know when to open and when to close.", aspects: ["Timely love", "Steady advance", "Labor's earnings", "Safe travels"] },
    { no: 28, grade: "中平", title: "Listening to the Pipa on the Xunyang River", titleZh: "浔阳江听琵琶", poem: "The boat moors at Xunyang under a moonlit night\nOne pipa tune moves the listener to pity\nLonging across two places - who will carry it\nWhite snow creeps to the temples' peak", poemZh: "船泊浔阳月夜天\n琵琶一曲动人怜\n相思两地凭谁寄\n白雪摧人上鬓巅", meaning: "Bai Juyi, moored at Xunyang, hears the pipa of a fellow exile - two castaways sharing a moment's comfort that cannot last. The great cycle of your fortune has yet to open, though brief bright spells appear. In work defend rather than attack; money comes hard, so economize seriously. In love look past appearances into the other's heart. Say little, keep composed, and wait for the wheel to turn.", aspects: ["Inner worth first", "Hold, don't attack", "Economize", "Lingering small ills"] },
    { no: 29, grade: "中吉", title: "Zhang Han Craves Autumn Perch", titleZh: "张翰思鲈", poem: "Perch sliced fine and chrysanthemums turning gold\nWine brimming in the cup to greet the evening cool\nRow out just as the tide runs high\nSuch a scene - joy without end", poemZh: "鲈鱼作脍菊花黄\n美酒盈樽迎晚凉\n泛棹正当潮上候\n这般佳景乐无央", meaning: "Zhang Han, feeling the autumn wind, resigns office and rows home for perch - contentment and timely retreat rather than grandeur. No vast riches this year, but peace, improving after autumn. Career can advance or withdraw as you please; refuse to chase money and it quietly arrives. Sweet romance and a year-end child are on the cards. For the contented heart, this stick promises genuinely happy days.", aspects: ["Sweet romance", "Advance or retreat", "Comes unbidden", "Watch digestion"] },
    { no: 30, grade: "下下", title: "Lady Yang's Demise", titleZh: "贵妃自缢", poem: "A beauty toppled kingdoms, enchanting all\nThe six palaces' painted faces, all unnamed\nAt the foot of Mawei her soul flew away\nLeaving the emperor in everlasting regret", poemZh: "倾国倾城媚百生\n六宫粉黛尽无名\n马嵬山下魂飞去\n至令明皇长恨情", meaning: "Lady Yang's first half is supreme favor, her second the silk at Mawei - rapture turning to ruin at splendor's peak. An unfavorable year: cash in while ahead. In business watch rivals and your own pride alike; defend wealth rather than risk it. Love faces layered tests - resist temptation - and indulgence in wine or pleasure saps health. Take the warning to heart and misfortune can still be dodged.", aspects: ["Tests await", "Quit while ahead", "Hold steady", "Shun wine, lust"] },
    { no: 31, grade: "下下", title: "Cai Zhongxing Meets Danger", titleZh: "蔡中兴遇险", poem: "Squall and sudden rain batter the boat's awning\nPeach blossoms by the stream fall wholly red\nThe fisherman startles from his spring dream\nPole in hand, he loses east and west", poemZh: "狂风骤雨打船篷\n溪畔桃花尽落红\n惊醒渔翁春梦熟\n持篙撑去失西东", meaning: "Cai Zhongxing's boat is caught mid-river by sudden weather: rain hammers the canopy, petals fall, the dreamer wakes with no idea which way to steer. Sudden perils multiply - raise your guard. Review work often so crises never catch you unprepared; if money must scatter, let it scatter into charity. See a doctor at the first symptom and travel carefully. Stay grounded and out of the limelight, and safety holds.", aspects: ["Storms spoil plans", "Review, prevent danger", "Charity deflects harm", "Treat at once"] },
    { no: 32, grade: "中平", title: "Su Wu Herding Sheep", titleZh: "苏武牧羊", poem: "Nineteen hard years by the northern sea\nThe tassel-fringed staff worn bare, chasing sand and dust\nSwallowing fur and snow - who pities me\nOnly the sheep remain for company", poemZh: "十九年前海上辛\n节旄凋败逐沙尘\n餐毛嚼雪谁怜我\n惟有羊儿作伴群", meaning: "Su Wu herds sheep nineteen years by the northern sea, staff in hand, refusing to bend - a stretch of grinding endurance that tests the will. You are still inside the hardship: found nothing new, and let nothing blow you off course. Money is scarce; persistence is the treasure. Love is severely tested, and marriage is best discussed after winter. Pile up merit, hold belief - late bloomers finish by going home.", aspects: ["Tests continue", "Hold unshaken", "Wealth scarce", "Minor ills, fine"] },
    { no: 33, grade: "中平", title: "Kongming Sees Through Cao Cao", titleZh: "孔明识破曹操", poem: "Cao Cao may plot deep and long\nBut wisdom cannot hide from Marquis Zhuge\nSee - he even borrows the east wind\nAnd wooden oxen, gliding horses, carry the grain", poemZh: "曹操虽有深谋计\n智慧难瞒诸葛侯\n试看东风都可借\n更能流马木成牛", meaning: "Zhuge Liang borrows the east wind and builds the wooden ox to out-think Cao Cao twice: straight wisdom defeats crooked cunning. Expect the unexpected - sudden events keep scrambling plans. Career sits on uneven ground; do things yourself, keep them aboveboard, and petty people keep their distance. Big money is possible, but only skill and nerve can seize it. At the first sign of illness, see a doctor at once.", aspects: ["Not the one", "Do it yourself", "Win on merit", "Seek help early"] },
    { no: 34, grade: "中吉", title: "Great Shun Plows Mount Li", titleZh: "大舜耕历山", poem: "Great Shun plowed the slopes of Mount Li\nHis heart still filial to two stubborn parents\nThe elephant plowing the field mirrors the home\nGood and evil stand clear right here", poemZh: "大舜虽耕在历山\n心常孝顺两嚣顽\n田中之象同家象\n善恶分明即此间", meaning: "Shun plows Mount Li while stubborn parents rage, yet his filial devotion moves heaven until elephants come to till for him - goodness repaid. A peaceful year sprinkled with real openings: love brings a kindred spirit and this is a fine year to marry; wealth arrives from its own quarter, unforced. Treat people kindly, honor your parents - when the household is at peace, every undertaking thrives.", aspects: ["Kindred hearts", "New paths open", "Wealth finds ways", "Broadly fine"] },
    { no: 35, grade: "中吉", title: "Tang Seng's Quest for the Scriptures", titleZh: "唐僧取经", poem: "Heaven lowers its charge upon this one\nFirst wearying bone and sinew, testing the body\nNever say the fine view comes easily\nPoverty and riches each have prior causes", poemZh: "天将降任此其人\n筋骨先劳苦彼身\n莫谓佳景来可易\n贫穷富贵有前因", meaning: "Tang Seng crosses a continent for scriptures: heaven first exhausts the body of the one it means to burden - bitter before sweet, tempered into an instrument. Plans grind and money lags right now, so refuse shortcuts and windfall temptations. Lengthen your view, keep good thoughts, and shrink from no labor. A destined partner appears, and marriage suits after autumn. Beyond the long hardship, reward waits at the far end.", aspects: ["Wed after autumn", "Will prevails", "No greed, haste", "Move, eat greens"] },
    { no: 36, grade: "中吉", title: "Xue Pinggui Returns Home", titleZh: "薛平贵归家", poem: "This matter is truly a boat come to shore\nWhy fear the wind and water unfinished\nRaise your head - the village ahead appears\nRound roof-corners, slanting sun, supper smoke rising", poemZh: "此事真如到岸船\n何忧风水不相全\n举头便见前村落\n屋角斜阳爨已烟", meaning: "Xue Pinggui returns in triumph to the kiln where his wife waits - boat at the bank, village smoke in sight: hardship ripening into reunion. Fortune climbs steadily from the year's start to its end. Set a long-horizon plan and walk it step by step; money arrives from its own quarter, small troubles aside. Lovers finally marry - never weigh a partner on scales of money. Home is blessed and calm.", aspects: ["Union at last", "Gently rising", "Wealth finds ways", "Old ills mend"] },
    { no: 37, grade: "上吉", title: "Dongpo at the Red Cliffs", titleZh: "东坡游赤壁", poem: "On the autumn river, moonlit night, angling for the great turtle\nThe catch shaped just like a four-gilled perch\nHome brew in plenty, a full measure in the jar\nPassing cups with friends until the pot runs dry", poemZh: "月夜秋江下钓鳌\n鱼形恰似四腮鲈\n家藏旧酿堪盈斗\n与友飞觞尽倒壶", meaning: "Su Dongpo drifts by moonlight beneath the Red Cliffs - autumn river, fresh catch, home brew, friends passing cups: season, place and company in tune. Keep the year in an optimistic key: career brings pleasant surprises and partnership suits you best; main and side income both flourish, so earn well and enjoy well. Heaven grants a fine match, with autumn a good wedding window. Only beware drinking past your measure.", aspects: ["Heaven-sent match", "Partner for profit", "Both channels thrive", "Mind your drinking"] },
    { no: 38, grade: "中吉", title: "Tao Yuanming Resigns His Office", titleZh: "陶渊明辞官", poem: "Home again - let office go, let leisure come\nA room scarce big for the knees is still enough\nBy the south window, proud and free, talk of poems and wine\nLeaning on a staff, wandering, drinking in the hills", poemZh: "归去来兮仕官闲\n室堪容膝亦为安\n南窗寄傲谈诗酒\n倚杖徘徊饱看山", meaning: "Tao Yuanming writes 'Home Again' and will not bow for five pecks of rice - a room that just fits the knees is peace enough. A calm year without big swings: start nothing new; consolidate. Income holds level, easing into better flow after winter. In romance two rhythms may not match - talk and yield more. Use the quiet to pick up one new craft; nothing here brings harm.", aspects: ["Adjust your rhythms", "Consolidate", "Better after winter", "Exercise more"] },
    { no: 39, grade: "中吉", title: "Bo Yi and Shu Qi Refuse Zhou Grain", titleZh: "夷齐耻食周粟", poem: "Bo Yi and Shu Qi could not stomach Zhou grain\nThe brothers gladly dined on mountain ferns\nYielding two thrones, their names last ten thousand ages\nYet, pitiable, they starved on Mount Shouyang", poemZh: "夷齐不忍食周粟\n兄弟心甘采蕨餐\n让国名应垂万古\n可怜饿倒首阳山", meaning: "Bo Yi and Shu Qi yield their kingdom and refuse the Zhou grain: integrity immortal, the body fallen on Shouyang - honor preserved past the point of survival. Openings exist this year but slip away to over-scrupulous holding. Build steadily; postpone wedding talk. Main income stays lean, side income occasional. Do not stake all on principle; consult family before big moves and keep fair-weather friends from your affairs.", aspects: ["No wedding talk", "Steady, solid steps", "Side work helps", "Watch stomach"] },
    { no: 40, grade: "下下", title: "Yu Boya Smashes His Qin", titleZh: "俞伯牙碎琴", poem: "How many soulmates can one lifetime hold\nHe smashed the qin, for Zhong Ziqi is gone to earth\nAt the grave a thousand streaming tears\nOne soul on either side of the dark divide", poemZh: "人世知音能有几\n碎琴都为子期忘\n坟前洒尽千行泪\n隔别阴阳各一方", meaning: "Yu Boya smashes his qin at his only listener's grave: a friend lost, a talent unheard - the grief of things ended. A hard year: avoid funerals and choose days even for hospital visits. Career marks time, moved only by your own effort; guard against loss and theft and shun speculation. Withdraw into study and self-cultivation for a season; keep the heart level and return when the hour turns.", aspects: ["Match hard-earned", "Withdraw and wait", "Guard against loss", "Soothe your heart"] },
    { no: 41, grade: "中吉", title: "Zhang Qian's Raft to the Milky Way", titleZh: "张骞月夜浮槎", poem: "The raft floats by moonlight to the River of Stars\nWhere he saw the heavenly maiden's weaving shuttle\nThe stone that props the loom, few men could name\nWho knew this treasure came from a nest of clouds", poemZh: "浮槎月夜到天河\n曾见天姬织锦梭\n石得支机人罕识\n那知此宝出云窝", meaning: "Zhang Qian's raft reaches the Milky Way and returns with a treasure no one recognizes - fortune held unknowingly, blessings that arrive by themselves. Everything points well; the year's end may add a delightful surprise. Handle career personally and press forward; wealth gathers without your noticing. This is a fine window for marriage - sweet romance succeeds easily. Make friends widely; helpful people are unusually many this year.", aspects: ["Sweet, easy success", "Press forward", "Gathers unseen", "Nothing to fear"] },
    { no: 42, grade: "中吉", title: "Wang Yun Offers Diaochan", titleZh: "王允献貂蝉", poem: "Strolling by moonlight to the flower railing\nNo stratagem yet to cut the traitor down\nBut Diaochan, minded to save the state, appears\nEven heroes fall at the beauty's pass", poemZh: "月明散步到花栏\n无策焉能剿灭奸\n幸有貂蝉思定国\n英雄难过美人关", meaning: "Wang Yun offers Diaochan and works the scheme that fells Dong Zhuo - hardship first, then a plan carried to perfection. Keep your own heart loyal and straight, and never wade in with the crooked. Beginnings will be hard; once a thread appears, success has begun. Romance fares well, with women best taking the initiative; both main and side money favor long positions over quick scores. Ignore momentary gains and losses.", aspects: ["Good for marriage", "Full effort", "Long positions", "Recovering well"] },
    { no: 43, grade: "下下", title: "Han Yu Demoted and Exiled", titleZh: "韩文公被贬", poem: "For blunt counsel that angered the throne\nDay and night he cannot leave the saddle\nMaster and servants gallop, spirit worn\nAnd heavier snow chokes the Lan Pass", poemZh: "只因直谏怒天颜\n昼夜难离在马鞍\n主仆奔忙神亦倦\n更加雪重拥蓝关", meaning: "Han Yu, demoted for honest remonstrance, rides day and night through snow-drifted passes - the road of duty blocked, hardship heaped on hardship. A difficult, obstruction-heavy year: guard against malicious hands, for timing and place are both against you - hold the last gate, goodwill. Money is scarce; live lean. The love road is bumpy; contest no one's ego. Preserve strength, keep the heart bright, and the turn will come.", aspects: ["Rocky road", "Hold goodwill", "Lean days", "Stay lighthearted"] },
    { no: 44, grade: "中吉", title: "The Flower Contest of the Tianbao Era", titleZh: "唐天宝评花", poem: "A garden full of spring vies in new dress\nAll seeming to contend for the national scent\nIn the end, who takes the crown of beauty\nThe peony outshines the hundred-flower field", poemZh: "满园春色斗新妆\n意似争妍夺国香\n到底是谁居丽首\n牡丹艳冠百花场", meaning: "In the Tianbao era the court judges flowers and the peony carries all before it - spring favor, first of rivals. The year improves after the spring equinox: career stands out from the crowd; push boldly while the wind is yours. Money runs smoother than before, main and side alike, though saving is wise against later trouble. Romance flourishes; marriage is favored. In triumph, new friends gather - keep the true ones.", aspects: ["Triumphant, marry", "Advance boldly", "Save within success", "Treat ills fast"] },
    { no: 45, grade: "中平", title: "Wang Zhi Meets the Immortals", titleZh: "王质遇仙", poem: "The woodcutter wanders, unmeaning, into cloud-country\nIdly watching two old immortals tap at chess\nHis axe-handle rots; he thinks of home\nSeven days on the mountain, a thousand years in the world", poemZh: "采樵不意到云天\n闲看敲棋二老仙\n柯烂也思归故里\n山中七日世千年", meaning: "Wang Zhi watches immortals at chess until his axe-handle rots - seven days in the hills, a thousand years gone below: time slips, chances fade. Opportunity hides inside your calm; miss the grasp and it wastes away, and the finest plan unrealized equals zero. Romance smiles - you may lose track of happy hours; wealth depends strictly on your own effort, or you return from a treasure mountain empty-handed. Act in time.", aspects: ["Lost in joy", "Seize the chance", "Effort earns", "Enjoy outdoors"] },
    { no: 46, grade: "下下", title: "Zuo Ci Teases Cao Cao", titleZh: "左慈戏曹操", poem: "Golden caskets offered up to Lord Cao\nSliced open - the fruit all hollow inside\nThe enraged tyrant swings his iron axe\nAnd the fugitive plunges into ten thousand sheep", poemZh: "黄金数盒献曹公\n剖看原来肉尽空\n怒动奸雄挥铁斧\n奔忙身入万羊中", meaning: "Zuo Ci's golden caskets prove hollow within as he slips the tyrant's axe amid ten thousand sheep: glittering surface hiding real danger. Not a good year - refuse to be blinded by outward sweetness. Contend step by careful step and watch for traps; money luck is dire, so touch no bargains. Dissolve danger with honesty and good deeds; harbor no reckless scheme, treat people generously, and harm turns aside.", aspects: ["Shifting illusions", "Tread carefully", "Refuse bargains", "Watch old ills"] },
    { no: 47, grade: "中平", title: "The Lord of Wu Demands Jingzhou", titleZh: "吴主索荆州", poem: "A thousand miles they come from western Shu\nTo ask: on what day will Jingzhou be returned\nLiu Bei, wordless, lets his tears speak\nRacking his mind, he wheels back toward Wu", poemZh: "遥遥千里来西蜀\n欲问荆州那日还\n刘备不言声泪下\n自思无策转吴间", meaning: "Liu Bei borrows Jingzhou and never returns it; the envoy's demand meets only silence and tears - a posture of being stuck, advance and retreat both blocked. Small misfortunes stalk the year: be scrupulous with loans and repayments, and refuse to act as middleman or guarantor. Business runs obstructed; opening a shop is unwise. Romance prickles over small matters; mind skin and stomach complaints. Better short pain than long - decide early.", aspects: ["Deadlocked quarrels", "No new venture", "Never guarantee", "Slow and recurring"] },
    { no: 48, grade: "中平", title: "Zhuo Wenjun Sells Wine", titleZh: "卓文君卖酒", poem: "From her boudoir she hears the qin and her thoughts take wing\nChanged to plain dress, midnight is sweetest\nYet there they are selling wine in Linqiong's market\nScholar and beauty, both in the kitchen", poemZh: "绣阁听琴自起思\n改妆夤夜最欢时\n可怜沽酒临邛市\n才子佳人两下厨", meaning: "Zhuo Wenjun elopes with Sima Xiangru, pouring wine in a market town - romance turning to labor, sweet start and workaday middle, all by their own hands. The year turns bitter to sweet, a great patron arriving in winter. Do things yourself; a joint venture is possible. Love luck runs high - do not miss the good match; there is no side money, every coin self-earned. Loosen the grip on the past.", aspects: ["Don't miss it", "Hands-on wins", "Self-earned only", "Cheerful, temperate"] },
    { no: 49, grade: "中吉", title: "Sima Xiangru Writes on the Bridge", titleZh: "司马相如题桥", poem: "Ten years of hard work beneath the window, complete\nYet ambition unspread, the vow not light\nSee the thirteen characters written on the bridge\nA lifetime's oath, fixed and true", poemZh: "十年窗下苦功成\n有志难舒愿不轻\n试看题桥十三字\n生平心誓确钟情", meaning: "Sima Xiangru vows on the bridge - no glory, no return - and keeps it: ten quiet years of toil, then the four-horse carriage. Days improve steadily, best after autumn. A rare chance to build from nothing - waste no time; mid-year main income swells with side money beside. Love is fulfilled; the one before you is the chosen one - propose. Leaving home to make your name fits perfectly now.", aspects: ["Fulfilled, within reach", "Build from nothing", "Both channels flow", "Spirits high"] },
    { no: 50, grade: "中吉", title: "Wu Zixu's Sword and the Fisherman", titleZh: "伍员赠剑渔父", poem: "Remember Wu Zixu in his year of flight\nFleeing, the crossing hopeless, till a fisherman appeared\nHe offered the treasured sword in thanks\nBut the righteous man refused the gift", poemZh: "记得当年伍子胥\n潜奔难渡幸逢渔\n欲将宝剑相持赠\n大义交朋却不辞", meaning: "Wu Zixu, hunted to the river, is ferried across by a fisherman who refuses his sword - help in hardship, righteousness between friends: danger turning to safety, a hand at the ford. Unrest on the surface hides a genuine opening. Promotion or raise cannot be forced, but firm resolve draws supporters by itself; a suitable partner is about to appear. Money arrives from its own quarter - renounce greed, never gamble.", aspects: ["Partner appears", "Danger turns safe", "No greed, bets", "Winter care"] },
    { no: 51, grade: "中平", title: "King Cheng Seals His Brother with a Leaf", titleZh: "成王剪桐封弟", poem: "Snipping a paulownia leaf was only child's play\nI seal you here - yet the word stood fast\nHow did jest harden into fact\nBecause a king's word knows no jokes", poemZh: "剪桐虽是作儿嬉\n封弟成圭语不移\n何以伪为成实事\n言因无戏故如斯", meaning: "Young King Cheng cuts a leaf into a jade tablet and playfully 'enfeoffs' his brother - the word, once given, is honored: a Son of Heaven does not jest. The year is plain, only small chances; do not overreach. Lovers quarrel - deal with each other honestly. Keep time and promises, plan before moving, bank strength for the future. Treat family and friends in good faith and betrayal will never find you.", aspects: ["Be candid", "Keep your word", "No great luck", "Mind limbs"] },
    { no: 52, grade: "中平", title: "Pangu Creates Heaven and Earth", titleZh: "盘古开辟天地", poem: "The light rose clear, the heavy sank below - heaven and earth\nClear and turbid congealed together, and there was man\nYou ask the stick to make things plain\nSo sort the three levels, fine and clear", poemZh: "上清下浊成天地\n清浊相凝便作人\n尔欲签求明白事\n且将三等细分明", meaning: "Pangu opens heaven and earth: the clear rises, the turbid sinks - fortune or failure is a choice left to you. The year rests on merit stored: sow good causes, reap good fruit; more labor, more gain; live by your own hands. There is no side money - amass wealth the slow way. Romance is unsteady; postpone engagement and wedding. Stay near good people, clear of the petty, and home stays safe.", aspects: ["Wait this year", "Labor earns", "No wagers", "Strong constitution"] },
    { no: 53, grade: "中吉", title: "Feng Xuan Serves Lord Mengchang", titleZh: "冯暖客孟尝", poem: "Three thousand guests in pearl-decked shoes filled Mengchang's hall\nWho among them knew the soaring hawk\nThe one who strummed his sword-hilt, singing, there\nThat was the hero whose resolve none could check", poemZh: "珠履三千客孟尝\n谁人识得有鹰扬\n其中弹铗归来者\n便是英雄志莫当", meaning: "Feng Xuan, one of three thousand retainers, strums his sword-hilt and sings his grievances - then wins Lord Mengchang's greatest victory: worth hidden in the crowd until its moment. Luck exists this year, but only for a moving mind. Secure harmony first - when above and below are at ease, good deeds carry plans to fulfillment. Mutual admiration colors romance; after autumn, marrying is apt. Relocation luck is strong; strangers become patrons.", aspects: ["Mutual admiration", "Harmony first", "Save steadily", "Sturdier than before"] },
    { no: 54, grade: "中平", title: "Zhuangzi Dreams of the Butterfly", titleZh: "庄周梦蝶", poem: "Zhuangzi, deep asleep, dreams he is a butterfly\nFluttering into a thicket of a hundred flowers\nHe gathers the heavenly fragrance and returns\nTo find himself still in his warm bed", poemZh: "庄子酣眠成蝶梦\n翩翻飞入百花丛\n天香采得归来后\n犹在高床暖枕中", meaning: "Zhuangzi dreams he is a butterfly among ten thousand flowers, gathers their fragrance, and wakes still between warm pillows - joy blurring the real and the dream. A settled, uneventful year, no time for grand designs: expect little from career; small money comes but will not pile up. Let love run its course and leave marriage for later. Do not grow dizzy amid praise - cultivate the heart and keep balance.", aspects: ["Let love run", "Nothing grand", "Hard to hoard", "Spirits bright"] },
    { no: 55, grade: "中平", title: "Wu Yinzhi Casts Away the Agarwood", titleZh: "吴隐之投沉香", poem: "The cove bears the agarwood's name, and an old regret\nCrossing the river, one remembers the ancient's heart\nHe cast his treasure in and resigned that day\nThe fragrance lingers, though hard to find", poemZh: "浦号沉香遗旧恨\n渡江犹忆古人心\n可怜当日辞官去\n虽有馨留不易寻", meaning: "Wu Yinzhi throws his agarwood into the river to prove his honesty - the fragrance remains, the fortune does not: integrity above profit. A steady year turning better; a job change may open, main income there for asking, but resist crooked windfalls. Love is hard to meet - let it come naturally; treat people sincerely and true friends gather. Guard against greed and entanglement; easy running does the body good.", aspects: ["Hard to meet", "A move possible", "Straight earnings", "Jog for health"] },
    { no: 56, grade: "中吉", title: "Lü Dongbin's Peachwood Sword", titleZh: "吕祖桃木剑", poem: "How do you know this sword will not become a dragon\nMeeting water, it must leap from the sleeve\nOne day it will soar ten thousand miles\nWith sinuous clouds attending it in the sky", poemZh: "安知此剑不成龙\n见水都应出袖中\n他日飞腾千万里\n上空妖娇有云从", meaning: "Lü Dongbin's peachwood sword waits in his sleeve until it meets water and turns to dragon: good fortune still brewing, improvement gathering force. The sword is on its way to mastery and things tilt toward the better: plans run smooth, and this is the hour to map the future. Those discussing marriage will surely succeed; money is slight but thickening. Rouse yourself, cultivate virtue, and great things take shape.", aspects: ["Marriage succeeds", "Plan the future", "Gradually rising", "Healing, no hindrance"] },
    { no: 57, grade: "中吉", title: "Winning the Flower Queen", titleZh: "独占花魁", poem: "The spring rain's patter just ended at the small tower\nClogs pace the street without pause\nThen the flower-seller's cry enters the lane\nOne branch bought, and a slow walk home", poemZh: "小楼春雨声初歇\n徘徊街头屐不停\n忽听卖花人入巷\n一枝买得慢慢行", meaning: "The oil peddler wins the Flower Queen through devotion - spring rain eased, one blossom bought, an unhurried walk home: first in line, then patient reaping. Luck turns with the spring equinox; more spring rain, better the year. Stay one step ahead, yet reap slowly once the deer is caught: career wants boldness with care; money stays modest, no craving. Marriage is right on time; health wants caution.", aspects: ["Right on time", "First, then steady", "Modest, no craving", "Caution first"] },
    { no: 58, grade: "下下", title: "Jian Shu's Unheeded Warning", titleZh: "蹇叔谏君", poem: "The Qin host shattered at Mount Yao\nThree commanders captured, then sent home\nJian Shu's counsel went unheard\nSpears reversed, armor shed, they straggled back to Qin", poemZh: "秦师大败在殽山\n三帅皆擒尽放还\n蹇叔谏言因不听\n倒戈舍甲返秦间", meaning: "Jian Shu weeps warning to an army marching to doom; the lord hears nothing, at Mount Yao the host is captured and shamed - the price of refusing counsel. A poor year: shun arrogance, disputes, lawsuits. In career defend, never attack - preserving the present is fortune. Guard romance against a third party; expect repeated money losses. Temper the heart, thin the desires, hear honest advice - that alone trims the damage.", aspects: ["Third-party risk", "Defend, don't attack", "Losses loom", "Simplicity heals"] },
    { no: 59, grade: "下下", title: "Dongshi Imitates a Frown", titleZh: "东施效颦", poem: "The silk-washing maiden's beauty had no twin\nIt charmed the King of Wu - and his kingdom fell\nWorst is Dongshi aping the frown\nCan the mountain pheasant outshine the phoenix", poemZh: "浣溪纱女美无双\n媚至吴王国破亡\n最恼东施效颦笑\n山鸡岂可胜鸾凰", meaning: "Xishi's frown was lovely; Dongshi's copy is comic - the mountain pheasant cannot pass as the phoenix: imitation gone wrong, weaknesses put on display. An unfavorable year: refine the heart, hide your shortcomings, and never push to the front. Money leaks - pare away pointless spending. In love beware false affection; heavy suspicion breeds its own ghosts. Stay put rather than relocate. Keep to your own gifts and safety holds.", aspects: ["False love, beware", "Keep your counsel", "Cut spending", "A trying passage"] },
    { no: 60, grade: "中平", title: "Li Bai Writes the Letter Drunk", titleZh: "李白醉和番书", poem: "The foreign letter answered in a drunken scrawl like cloud-smoke\nHis days spent sleeping in Chang'an taverns\nShould the emperor's summons arrive\nTwice called, he will not board the magnolia boat", poemZh: "和番醉笔似云烟\n日在长安酒店眠\n倘遇唐皇颁令召\n重呼不上木兰船", meaning: "Li Bai answers the foreign court's letter dead drunk - and makes a grandee polish his ink: towering talent, unbroken pride, content without favor. No large openings this year, and appearances deceive. Small success must not go to the head - hold your post; part-time income may out-earn the main. An admirer keeps signaling - test the sincerity. Want little, live cheerfully, skip vanity and the extra cups.", aspects: ["Test sincerity", "Hold your post", "Side work pays", "Mind the drinking"] },
    { no: 61, grade: "下下", title: "Twelve Gold Medals Recall Yue Fei", titleZh: "十二金牌召岳飞", poem: "Twelve gold tablets summon him swiftly back\nWhen will the scheming traitor turn to ash\nIn one morning a lifetime's merit scatters\nOld and young cling to the cart, weeping without end", poemZh: "十二金牌速召回\n奸雄设计几时灰\n可怜一旦功劳散\n老少扶车不断哀", meaning: "Twelve gold tablets recall Yue Fei at victory's eve - a schemer undoes ten years of merit on success's threshold. A year of hard choices: make no sudden moves; the grand plan looks right but rings false - force nothing. Money may need spending to avert calamity; mind fraud and theft. Spouses slip into suspicion - petty people fan it. Store merit, keep good ties, hear counsel; extra care in autumn and winter.", aspects: ["Curb suspicion", "Hold, don't advance", "Fraud and theft", "Autumn-winter care"] },
    { no: 62, grade: "中平", title: "Confucius Declines Office", titleZh: "孔子不仕", poem: "A fine jade lies wrapped and stored in its case\nNo need to haggle for a better price\nSell it if you will - the right buyer waits\nWhy must this treasure keep appraising itself", poemZh: "美玉于斯韫匮藏\n休求善价费商量\n沽之亦可随相待\n此物何须自看常", meaning: "Confucius, out of office, likens himself to jade in its box: waiting for the right buyer, never selling cheap because no one yet knows. You carry great fortune, but the hour has not come. Until recognition arrives, keep the old path, polish yourself, trim expenses, and widen income. Marriage should not be rushed; after a move, surroundings improve. Hold big aims; when the moment lands, the jade meets its connoisseur.", aspects: ["No rushing", "Polish and keep", "Trim, widen income", "Slow recovery"] },
    { no: 63, grade: "中吉", title: "Yan Hui Finds Joy in Poverty", titleZh: "颜回乐道安贫", poem: "A mean lane, a basket of rice, a gourd of water - no cause for grief\nBystanders see it and worry sore\nThey know not: joy in the Way forgets poverty\nThe second Sage's name endures forever", poemZh: "陋巷箪瓢不足愁\n旁人见此甚为忧\n不知乐道忘贫乏\n亚圣芳名万古留", meaning: "Yan Hui lives on a bowl of rice and a gourd of water in a poor lane, joy unchanged - contentment itself, and a name that outlasts dynasties. A steady year flecked with lucky moments: income arrives unchased; do not change trades - hold and develop. This is a good year to marry; someone already admires your character and gifts. Eat light and plain; mind small skin and stomach complaints.", aspects: ["Admired for character", "Hold, don't switch", "Income unbidden", "Eat light"] },
    { no: 64, grade: "中吉", title: "Meng Zhifan Covers the Retreat", titleZh: "孟之反殿师", poem: "Covering a routed army - remember the ancient\nHe enters the gate on horseback, claiming no skill\nWho willingly rides last for a beaten host\nMy horse is spent, he says - taking no credit", poemZh: "奔殿须知上古人\n入门策马不夸能\n败师谁肯甘从后\n托谓鸣骢畏苦辛", meaning: "Meng Zhifan rides rearguard for a defeated army, then enters the gate last, crediting his horse: duty done, honors declined. A year of plowing, not harvest. Career meets small obstructions one after another - clear them and the view brightens; small expenses run many, big money stays out. Romance repeats and quarrels by turns; don't crush yourself with pressure - take setbacks and misunderstandings lightly, and the household fortune is excellent.", aspects: ["Repeats and spats", "Plowing year", "Small sums out", "Ease the pressure"] },
    { no: 65, grade: "下下", title: "The Consort Hides in the Well", titleZh: "胭脂井藏妃", poem: "As Sui extinguished Chen, the halberds clashed\nAll because enchantment closed the sovereign's eyes\nFleeing east and west, nowhere to hide\nIn the well, the rouge hides the jade one", poemZh: "隋灭陈时戟伐纷\n都因妖媚闭明君\n东奔西赴无藏息\n井里胭脂隐玉人", meaning: "The last ruler of Chen, lost in pleasure, hides with his consort in the Well of Rouge as the dynasty falls - indulgence breeding ruin, nowhere left to hide. The odds run bad - wake early: drown no further in wine and pleasure, or regret comes too late. Work blocks at every turn - check impatience; beware honeyed schemes. Even losing money to avert disaster counts as fortune. Take heed; pile up merit.", aspects: ["No outside affairs", "Curb impatience", "Paying averts harm", "No wine, lust"] },
    { no: 66, grade: "上吉", title: "Gathering of Sages at the Orchid Pavilion", titleZh: "羲之会群贤", poem: "At the Orchid Pavilion the sages gather\nCups float down the winding stream, strings set aside\nSky bright, air clear, the breeze mild and free\nTall bamboos in deep grove - joy at ease", poemZh: "兰亭雅会众群贤\n曲水流觞舍管弦\n天朗气清风惠畅\n茂林修竹乐怡然", meaning: "Wang Xizhi's Orchid Pavilion gathering: worthies assembled, cups drifting down the winding stream, sky clear and breeze mild - a hundred things auspicious. A greatly fortunate year, luck already knocking; from late spring into early summer a major turn arrives. Career enjoys timing, place and people at once; money streams in from four directions. A cheerful, kindly partner is worth a lifelong pledge; spirits so high illness hardly lands.", aspects: ["Pledge for life", "Great turn coming", "Wealth all around", "Illness hardly lands"] },
    { no: 67, grade: "中平", title: "Li Yuanba the Unmatched", titleZh: "李元霸称雄", poem: "None could withstand such strength as his\nYet never lean on heroics to top the field\nOne might hoist Mount Tai and leap the Northern Sea\nBut body and life still outweigh all", poemZh: "人虽勇力不能当\n莫恃英雄独冠场\n可挟泰山超北海\n身心犹贵重存亡", meaning: "Li Yuanba, strongest of his age, dies young at his peak - unchecked might spends the self: a warning against flashing edges. Calm on the surface, risk gathers beneath. Career cannot run on drive alone - think, plan, look three times before moving. No impulsive wedding; guard against fierce quarrels. Move carefully, mind accidents and small hurts to limbs. Gather in the sharpness; body and life come first.", aspects: ["No impulsive vows", "Think thrice", "Small gains only", "Mind the road"] },
    { no: 68, grade: "中吉", title: "Jiang Taigong Meets King Wen", titleZh: "姜公遇文王", poem: "Long has he held cloud-high ambition, unfurled not yet\nRod on shoulder, fishing the Wei River\nKing Wen comes a thousand li seeking the wise\nZhou rises, Shang falls, all as he wills", poemZh: "久抱凌云志未舒\n荷竿渭水钓游鱼\n文王千里求贤士\n灭纣兴周任意如", meaning: "Jiang Taigong fishes the Wei with a straight hook until King Wen comes a thousand li - long constraint breaking open, a worthy finally meeting his lord. Career enters smoother ground, a grand patron lifting you; a wish held for years draws near. Love's hour is now, the bond solid as fish in water. Money there is, but temper it - no extravagance. Emigration or relocation holds great promise.", aspects: ["Deep, easy bond", "Patron lifts you", "Wealth, no waste", "Balance work, rest"] },
    { no: 69, grade: "中吉", title: "Han Yu Sacrifices to the Crocodiles", titleZh: "韩文公祭鳄鱼", poem: "Ten years in office with loyalty and duty at heart\nRich harvests, a happy people, kindness unforgotten\nEven the crocodiles' poison is stilled\nBy prayer to the lords of river and sea", poemZh: "忠义存心官十载\n年丰民乐惠难忘\n鳄鱼毒害都能息\n祷告长江北海王", meaning: "Han Yu writes a proclamation and sacrifices to the river, and the man-eating crocodiles withdraw - sincerity and firm resolve turning peril into safety. A good year - a kind heart makes it better still. Work runs smoothly; a more challenging post may suit you. Money luck is excellent, main and side alike, with a small windfall beside. Long knowing ends in sincere marriage. Exercise often, treat people truly, and friends multiply.", aspects: ["Sincerity succeeds", "Smooth, may transfer", "Both channels good", "Exercise more"] },
    { no: 70, grade: "中平", title: "The Old Man Loses His Horse", titleZh: "塞翁失马", poem: "Just like the old man at the frontier long ago\nWho lost his horse midway on the road\nWho can say which is fortune, which is disaster\nOnly at the end is the whole tale clear", poemZh: "可比当年一塞翁\n虽然失马半途中\n不知祸福真何事\n到底方明事始终", meaning: "The old man loses his horse; the horse returns leading a fine herd - blessing and bane trade places, gains and losses reverse. The year swings often, so shrug off the passing score. Career wants steady tilling, no great expansion; money comes and goes. In love, meetings and partings shift - no wedding talk until you truly know each other. Meet change with stillness; doers of good see harm turn to help.", aspects: ["Come and go", "Steady tilling", "In and out", "Minor ills only"] },
    { no: 71, grade: "中平", title: "Zhuangzi Revives the Stranded Fish", titleZh: "庄周活鲋鱼", poem: "In the dried wheel-rut a fish lies trapped\nIts fate can be read right there and then\nBut draw the West River's water to it\nAnd who knows - a dragon one day", poemZh: "涸辙之中鲋困之\n穷通自可卜当时\n若能引得西江水\n他日成龙也未知", meaning: "The stranded fish begs a dipper of water; Zhuangzi promises the whole West River - present want against future rescue. Timing and place run against you; endure and win the human factor. Do not steer career by wish alone; keeping to your post is the way. Money stays stalled save small spring-autumn catches; mind your conduct wherever disputes could stir. Should a great patron appear, dragon-hood is not impossible.", aspects: ["Await help", "Keep the post", "Spring-autumn gains", "Fruit and greens"] },
    { no: 72, grade: "中平", title: "Waiting by the Stump for a Rabbit", titleZh: "宋人守株待兔", poem: "Waiting, waiting for the rabbit - what comes of it\nSigh at the fool who guards the stump\nSuch uselessness makes me laugh\nNo need to stand rigid, bound by the old ways", poemZh: "兔儿久待意如何\n堪叹愚人独守株\n算是无能令我笑\n不须守旧自拘拘", meaning: "A farmer sees a rabbit crash dead against a stump and abandons his fields to wait for the next - routine mistaken for strategy. No great harm, but no great deeds either; the run stays level until fortune moves. Regular income is flat - do not build hopes on small windfalls. Do today's work well while you watch for the opening, and widen your circle to seed the future.", aspects: ["Marriage on hold", "Hold and seek", "No lucky windfalls", "Change doctors"] },
    { no: 73, grade: "上上", title: "The Top Scholar Returns in Glory", titleZh: "状元衣锦荣归", poem: "Flowers line the road, scenting the hooves\nThe blue scholar's robe exchanged for brocade\nAlong the streets the fair ones vie in envy\nHis name lifted high on the Wild Goose Pagoda", poemZh: "夹道花香衬马蹄\n蓝袍改换锦衣归\n满街红粉皆争羡\n翘首芳名雁塔题", meaning: "The new top scholar rides home in brocade, fragrance lining the road, his name carved on the Goose Pagoda - fame and fortune in flower. Everything runs to wish: career climbs another story with money rolling in; marrying and moving both favored, the household turns prosperous, a fine son on the way; study reaches the head of the class. No serious illness - only temper the banqueting. Press the winning streak.", aspects: ["Match arrived", "Rising and thriving", "All channels rich", "Temper the feasting"] },
    { no: 74, grade: "下下", title: "Zhu Maichen Divorces His Wife", titleZh: "朱买臣分妻", poem: "Remember the lean years when luck ran dry\nHusband and wife at odds, torn in two\nHis name on the Goose Pagoda, he returns\nWater poured out before the horse, grief too late", poemZh: "回忆当年运蹇时\n夫妻反目两分离\n名题雁塔归来后\n覆水马头时否悲", meaning: "Zhu Maichen's wife, weary of poverty, leaves him; when he returns in honor, the poured water cannot be gathered again - devotion bent by hardship, regret waiting at the top. Heaven's timing runs against you, so plan long: no get-rich-quick moves - steady digging is already good fortune. Romance stirs waves that can split on the rocks; tend your character, keep the heart bright. In hardship, true feeling finally shows.", aspects: ["Rocks in romance", "Dig steadily", "Hold the line", "Keep spirits bright"] },
    { no: 75, grade: "下下", title: "Lun Wenxu and His Wife", titleZh: "伦文叙戏妻", poem: "How can marriage resent a poor house\nLun Wenxu and his wife split apart\nThen, first on the dragon-and-tiger roll\nHis mocking wife falls from the tower and dies", poemZh: "婚姻岂可厌家贫\n文叙夫妻两拆分\n一旦首登龙虎榜\n戏妻楼坠自身亡", meaning: "Lun Wenxu's wife, scornful of poverty, remarries - then he tops the national roll and her taunt ends in a fatal fall: the cruelest of the hundred, short sight forging its own ruin. Hold the old and quiet this year; career will find its dawn if you wait. Never weigh a partner in scales of money, nor change heart over poverty. Refuse quarrels and quick profit; check any stubborn illness thoroughly.", aspects: ["Never forsake", "Hold for dawn", "Little to seek", "Check thoroughly"] },
    { no: 76, grade: "中平", title: "Cultivating Virtue in Poverty", titleZh: "修身不厌贫", poem: "Delight in the Way, and cultivate the self\nPlain water, a bent arm for a pillow - who resents poverty\nRiches and rank won by injustice\nAre, to my heart, but drifting clouds", poemZh: "人能乐道自修身\n疏水曲肱岂厌贫\n不义而富且贵者\n我心都作是浮云", meaning: "Confucius on plain water and a bent arm for a pillow: joy in the Way leaves no room to resent poverty, and ill-gotten splendor is only passing cloud. Circumstances run plain, even lean, but keeping to the straight path and refining yourself brings its own peace. Career and money have yet to flourish - fill the time growing yourself and waiting well. A clear conscience carries you safely toward the turn.", aspects: ["Marry later", "Cultivate, keep place", "Light on profit", "Content, healthy"] },
    { no: 77, grade: "中平", title: "Gongye Chang Jailed", titleZh: "公冶长入狱", poem: "Gongye Chang understood the speech of birds\nFrom the south mountain: a tiger dragging a sheep\nThough his body sat in ropes and chains\nIn the end the harm was none of his doing", poemZh: "鸟语能通公冶长\n南山得个虎拖羊\n其身虽在于缧绁\n到底非关自己殃", meaning: "Gongye Chang, who understood bird talk, fetches the tiger's abandoned sheep and lands in jail for theft - bound and blamed, yet blameless to the end. Disputes cling to you this year, and gossip is usually the rope: beware of meddlers carrying tales. When conflict comes, endure and let the truth clear itself - it will. Say little, do much, move with care, and you pass through unharmed.", aspects: ["Mind your words", "Disputes cling", "Refuse windfalls", "Small ills only"] },
    { no: 78, grade: "上吉", title: "Zeng Dian Speaks His Aspiration", titleZh: "曾点论志", poem: "The zither fades with one last clang, its echo holding\nLate spring, and the new spring robes just ready\nFive or six grown, six or seven children\nBathed at the rain altar, singing all the way home", poemZh: "瑟希铿尔尚留声\n春暮时刚春服成\n冠五六人童六七\n舞雩归咏畅幽情", meaning: "Asked his ambition, Zeng Dian answers: a late-spring outing with friends, bathing in the Yi, catching the breeze at the rain altar, chanting poems home - unhurried harmony. The year runs smooth and warm; most wishes find their form. Marriage settles sweetly, the household rests easy; plans ripen when the season serves. Move at an easy pace and things fall into place - only do not let ease slide into idleness.", aspects: ["Sweet union", "Unhurried success", "Favorable flows", "Refreshed and easy"] },
    { no: 79, grade: "中平", title: "Zhang Liang Awakens to the Way", titleZh: "张良悟道", poem: "Riches and rank are a ripe spring dream\nWhy must the world fight so hard for them\nLet him stand at court with tablet in hand\nAt death, one cupful of earth remains", poemZh: "富贵有如春梦熟\n世人何苦力争求\n任他秉笏当朝立\n到死惟留土一杯", meaning: "Zhang Liang, his work done, walks away to follow Master Red Pine - wealth seen clear as a spring dream. Do not strain after name and profit: the world wrestles for a court seat, and the end of that row is one cup of earth. Take things lightly, keep to your measure; press forward greedy and you only fray yourself. A step back opens the whole sky; calm preserves health.", aspects: ["Let it flow", "Rank lightly", "Enough is enough", "Calm keeps well"] },
    { no: 80, grade: "中吉", title: "Yue Guang Dissolves the Doubt", titleZh: "乐广释疑", poem: "Cups fly, dancers face each other - how long the revel\nA bow's reflection in the cup, mistaken for a snake\nOnce the riddle of the poem is read\nWorst turns to best, without a slip", poemZh: "飞觞对舞几时赊\n弓影横杯误作蛇\n猜透诗中元妙诀\n泰来否极事无差", meaning: "Yue Guang's guest sees a snake in his wine - only the bow's reflection - and recovers the moment the doubt dissolves. Most of what frightens you is self-made shadow; the truth is not half so bad. Trace the recent trouble to its source: once the knot unties, the heart opens. In love, misunderstandings want honest talk, not suspicion left to grow. Clear the fog, and the good turn arrives on schedule.", aspects: ["Doubt misleads", "Truth dawning", "Doubts dissolve", "Wide heart heals"] },
    { no: 81, grade: "中吉", title: "The Hen Pheasant Knows Her Hour", titleZh: "雌雉朝圣", poem: "On the mountain beam the hen pheasant finds her hour\nFlying up and down, calling, delighting in herself\nShe starts up first, then settles after flight\nThrice snuffing the air, she crosses the slope", poemZh: "山梁雌雉得其时\n上下飞鸣自乐之\n色举须知翔后集\n作声三嗅过山欹", meaning: "The hen pheasant on the ridge knows her hour: she rises at the first sign of danger, circles, and only then settles - timely sense, peril read and dodged. Weigh the hour before you move, and where danger shows itself, step aside - fortune keeps a place for the alert. Changes are in the air: decide promptly rather than drift, keep advance and retreat in balance, and leave margin against triumphs curdling.", aspects: ["Wait your hour", "Read the moment", "Expect surprises", "Balanced movement"] },
    { no: 82, grade: "中平", title: "Confucius Plays the Chime Stones", titleZh: "孔子击磬", poem: "The Sage taps his chime-stones in Wei\nWho could guess a basket-bearer pauses at the gate\nHe sighs: one heart trying to hold up a failing Way\nPity - the sun and moon are passing now", poemZh: "圣人击磬在于卫\n谁料过门有荷篑\n嗟叹有心挽道穷\n可怜日月今将逝", meaning: "Confucius plays his chime-stones in Wei; a passing hermit reads the music: a heart laboring to save a sinking Way as the days run out. Great aims meet no audience yet - make the hours count: set the goal and act early, before the light spends itself. Keep the ideal and a clear conscience; uncrowned for a season, the turn will still come. Only mind ideals not wearing the body out.", aspects: ["Audience scarce", "Act early", "Watch the drain", "Don't overwork"] },
    { no: 83, grade: "中平", title: "Chisongzi Calls One to the Hills", titleZh: "赤松子招隐", poem: "In this dusty world, when has the body known rest\nWorldly affairs pile up like mountain on mountain\nRich already, yet grieving for a noble son\nUnnoticed, flowers open and flowers fade", poemZh: "凡尘身历几时闲\n世事浑如叠叠山\n既富尚忧无贵子\n不知花放又花残", meaning: "Master Red Pine calls the seeker out of the dust: even the rich man grieves for a noble heir - the world is never complete, and the race for name and profit ages people early. Contentment is this year's medicine: do not chase rank and riches, and heart and body stay well. Insist on completeness and worry moves in for good. Step back, keep the peace, take days as they come.", aspects: ["Let it flow", "Contentment first", "Do not force", "Nurture yourself"] },
    { no: 84, grade: "中吉", title: "Han Xin Leaves Chu for Han", titleZh: "韩信弃楚归汉", poem: "A belly full of genius, ambition not yet aloft\nCould not lift the iron cock, given no room\nZhang Liang pointed the way - he bet on Han\nXiang Yu at the Wu River met his end", poemZh: "满腹奇才志未冲\n铁鸡难举意无容\n张良指示身投汉\n项羽乌江命自穷", meaning: "Han Xin, unused under Chu, follows Zhang Liang's pointer to Han, made grand general on a raised altar, helping found the empire - hard first, easy after. Present dullness means the hour, not the man: your pearl has yet to meet its buyer. A patron's direction can turn you onto the right road; persistence flips everything - changing jobs or scenes holds the turn. Never write yourself off over one flat season.", aspects: ["Another door opens", "Better ground ahead", "The turn comes", "Cheerful and well"] },
    { no: 85, grade: "上吉", title: "Taiyi's Lamp for the Scholar", titleZh: "太乙燃藜", poem: "Taiyi kindles the goosefoot staff to light the scholar's books\nTen years of hard toil beneath the window unfurl\nBrows lifted, spirits high, brocade on his back\nFour horses, a tall carriage, crowds lining the road", poemZh: "太乙燃藜照读书\n十年窗下苦功舒\n扬眉吐气袍穿锦\n驷马高车拥道随", meaning: "The spirit Taiyi lights his staff so Liu Xiang can study through the night - and ten patient years end in brocade robes and a four-horse carriage. Sturdy labor is about to be paid in splendor: study leaps ahead, career rises high, fame and profit both arrive. Seize the moment and ride it; only keep greed on a short leash. The road ahead is bright almost without limit.", aspects: ["Heaven-sent match", "Fame achieved", "Main fortune swells", "Thriving health"] },
    { no: 86, grade: "中平", title: "Tao Kan's Mother Welcomes Guests", titleZh: "侃母迎宾", poem: "She cut her own hair to welcome a guest - poor as she was\nWhere else a worthy woman in such poverty\nAncient or modern, only Tao Kan's mother\nAnd so her name rings down ten thousand generations", poemZh: "截发迎宾否也贫\n贫中贤妇更何人\n古今只有陶侃母\n所以名留万代闻", meaning: "Tao Kan's mother cuts off her hair to sell for wine when a guest arrives - poor in means, matchless in virtue, remembered for ages. Means are thin for now, but keeping faith with virtue and duty brings the first shoots of recovery. Repay every kindness; act with honesty and diligence, and the household stays safe while your name quietly rises. Hold steady through this stretch of days.", aspects: ["Choose by virtue", "Keep duty, wait", "Hard-earned money", "Safe and sound"] },
    { no: 87, grade: "中平", title: "Xun and Lu Trade Wit", titleZh: "荀陆座谈", poem: "On the flowered seats they parade their heroics\nBut in the end, who holds perfect fairness\nOne cries: the crane that calls beneath the sun\nThe other: the dragon amid the clouds", poemZh: "会谈华座逞英雄\n究竟谁人秉大公\n一云日下荀鸣鹤\n一说云间陆士龙", meaning: "Xun Yin and Lu Yun trade boasts across the hall - the crane beneath the sun against the dragon among the clouds - brilliance spent on a contest of tongues. Do not fight for the last word this year: much speech invites error and gossip follows. Yield the argument, broaden your bearing; solid ground underfoot beats any victory of words, and one careless phrase costs real trouble. Let the work speak.", aspects: ["Speak little", "Gossip invites trouble", "Beware the con", "Keep calm"] },
    { no: 88, grade: "中吉", title: "Hua Mulan Joins the Army", titleZh: "花木兰从军", poem: "Taking her father's place at war - what daring courage\nHow many women ever matched the bearded brave\nServing the realm with her body - loyal and filial\nThe grand lords of the day laughed to shame", poemZh: "替父从军胆气雄\n须眉巾帼几人同\n以身报国忠而孝\n笑煞当时众钜公", meaning: "Hua Mulan takes her father's place in the army, serves through long campaigns, and comes home covered in honor - loyalty and filial duty carried through fire. Take up your responsibility the same way: hardship first, glory after, and danger tamed by commitment. Family and calling can both be served - hold the conviction, meet it bravely, and general esteem follows. Ignore the early laughter; time settles every account of value.", aspects: ["Loyal and filial", "Danger turns safe", "Thrift builds wealth", "Toil then ease"] },
    { no: 89, grade: "下下", title: "Ji Zha Hangs Up His Sword", titleZh: "吴季子挂剑", poem: "Far from home he wears the fish-gut sword\nWho knew the Lord of Xu silently desired it\nReturning, he means to give it as promised\nAnd hangs it on the tree beside the grave", poemZh: "他乡远历佩鱼肠\n谁料徐君意欲将\n既返愿为相赠答\n且悬树下表情长", meaning: "Ji Zha had silently promised his sword to the Lord of Xu; returning too late, he hangs it on the grave tree - a promise kept past death, though the year runs against him. Fine intentions meet obstruction; what honor gives away drains the purse. Proceed carefully, protect what is built, advance nothing new. Keep faith with people - but keep something back for yourself, and guard against illness and theft.", aspects: ["Blocked affairs", "Nothing completes", "Losses drain", "Hidden ills"] },
    { no: 90, grade: "中平", title: "Hongfu Elopes by Night", titleZh: "红拂女私奔", poem: "Touching up her fading makeup, ready to flee by night\nIn that hall, who else was Li Jing\nWho knew the Bearded One, love-struck\nThrice drew his sword - and never dared speak", poemZh: "细整残妆夜欲奔\n座中李靖更何人\n那知虬髯情钟处\n拔剑三回未敢陈", meaning: "Hongfu's sharp eye picks Li Jing from the crowd and she flees with him by night; the Curly-Bearded hero, smitten, thrice half-draws his sword and thrice thinks better of it. The hour is unripe and feelings run high - in love above all, watch coolly before leaping. Forbear rather than lunge; weigh it deeply, then act. Let the situation clear before committing, and a mismatch is spared you.", aspects: ["Wait for clarity", "Forbear, don't rush", "Hold steady", "Curb the fire"] },
    { no: 91, grade: "上上", title: "Chang'e in the Moon Palace", titleZh: "月里嫦娥", poem: "In the toad palace and moon halls, cassia drifts fragrance\nThe jade mirror, round and whole, lights ten thousand miles\nSix waters and three hills gather in the glass\nOne flawless disc hung on the farthest sky", poemZh: "蟾宫月殿桂飘香\n玉箧团圆万里光\n六水三山归镜里\n无瑕一片挂穹苍", meaning: "Chang'e keeps the palace of the moon: cassia fragrance, a round bright mirror, ten thousand miles of flawless light - among the luckiest of all hundred sticks, an emblem of nobility and completeness. Everything is favored: marriage becomes a union made in heaven, no wish fails, and fame and profit come together. Advance with the season - the road ahead is almost limitless. Only carry humility at that height.", aspects: ["Union made above", "All things favor", "Fame and profit", "Long, healthy joy"] },
    { no: 92, grade: "中吉", title: "Confucius Hears the Shao Music", titleZh: "孔子闻韶乐", poem: "The Utmost Sage journeyed through the states\nIn Qi he heard the Shao music played\nThree months passed - he tasted no meat's savor\nHow perfect - and the great Way stood complete", poemZh: "至圣周游列国行\n在齐得听奏韶乐\n三月不知嘉肉味\n善哉大道可功成", meaning: "Confucius hears the Shao in Qi and for three months loses the taste of meat - such absorption, such praise of perfect beauty. Concentration is this term's whole secret: the chance stands before you, but must be taken, not admired. Long-acquainted couples may rightly speak of marriage; career wants a new front opened on momentum. Money arrives slowly - no short-term speculation - and regular hours spare the stomach.", aspects: ["Marry this year", "Good stretch coming", "Steady gains", "Mind digestion"] },
    { no: 93, grade: "下下", title: "Confucius Hears the Music of Zheng and Wei", titleZh: "孔子闻郑卫之音", poem: "The music of Zheng and Wei cannot be borne\nLewd airs corrupt custom; the state nears collapse\nIt leads one deep into the lost ford\nNothing played resembles the ancient tone", poemZh: "郑卫之音不忍听\n淫风败俗国将倾\n令人深入迷津路\n所奏全非古乐声", meaning: "Confucius covers his ears at the music of Zheng and Wei: seductive, corrupting, a state's ruin set to tune - a stick warning of the lost road. Temptation dresses beautifully this year, and the near path bends toward the mire. Refuse indulgence - wine, pleasure, fair-weather companions included; distance the enticers and turn back early, and harm gives way to good. Keep household disputes quiet; walk in the open.", aspects: ["Resist temptation", "Turn back now", "Nothing gathers", "Beware wine, lust"] },
    { no: 94, grade: "中平", title: "The Curly-Bearded Guest Sails to Fuyu", titleZh: "髯公远走扶余", poem: "One den cannot hold two tiger cubs\nRiding the wind to other ridges, each settles apart\nKeeping a famous mountain for a den\nEscapes the mauling - and the late regret", poemZh: "一窟难容两虎儿\n乘风别岭各栖之\n名山自守为巢穴\n可免伤残后悔迟", meaning: "The Curly-Bearded Guest sees in Li Shimin the lord to come - one mountain cannot seat two tigers - and sails away on the wind to found his own kingdom at Fuyu. Read the landscape the same way: where present ground cannot stretch your gifts, change ground and build again. No clinging contests with the strong; yielding opens a new world, and distant fields yield better harvests than stubborn ones.", aspects: ["Another path", "A move pays", "Fortune far afield", "Move freely"] },
    { no: 95, grade: "中平", title: "Nüwa Mends the Sky", titleZh: "女娲炼石补天", poem: "Diligence, basket by basket, builds a mountain\nFrom little to much - never mind the tedium\nYou who flinch at toil and stop at your own line\nEven mending heaven with smelted stone holds no terror", poemZh: "功勤一篑可成山\n由少而多莫惮烦\n作事畏辛今汝画\n补天炼石亦无难", meaning: "Nüwa smelts stones to mend the broken sky - each basket of earth adds to a mountain, and the patient pile becomes the great work. Persistence beats dullness, but the year's trap is quitting: fear of hardship at the half-way line leaves everything begun and nothing done. Shrink from no trouble, keep at it, and even sky-mending comes within reach. Consolidate steadily and expect no overnight arrival.", aspects: ["Effort covers", "Little to much", "No shortcuts", "Pace your labor"] },
    { no: 96, grade: "中平", title: "The Wanderer Longs for Home", titleZh: "游子思家", poem: "The Qiang flute sounds again, its air still sadder\nA sojourner far from home feels the homing season stir\nThe lone goose flying south, as if in pity\nPlease carry this letter home for me", poemZh: "羌笛频吹韵更悲\n异乡作客触归期\n南来孤雁如怜我\n烦寄家书转达知", meaning: "The wanderer in a strange land hears the frontier flute and aches: home is far, the homing season stirs, and only the southbound goose can carry word. Longing runs deep this year while affairs drag and wishes fray. Hold your present post and make no sudden moves; the autumn-winter passage wants particular care. Keep the household safe - reunion has its own date, and the date will keep.", aspects: ["Meetings in time", "Affairs drag", "Toil and moil", "Mind the road"] },
    { no: 97, grade: "中平", title: "Kangshun Goes Fishing", titleZh: "康顺钓鱼", poem: "Leaning on the rail of the south tower at dusk\nThe whole view - scenery deep and still\nA little boat casts its bait again and again\nDid the old fisherman catch a fish, or no", poemZh: "凭栏晚眺倚南楼\n满目风光景色幽\n一叶小舟频下饵\n渔翁钓得有鱼不", meaning: "Evening from the south tower: flawless scenery, one small boat dropping bait again and again - whether anything bites, the poem never says. The view is lovely; the catch is uncertain. Fame and profit are bait, and the take is not yours to command: follow conditions, don't force - spring and autumn hold the best odds. Keep to the ordinary and peace holds; grasp too hard, the hand closes on nothing.", aspects: ["Let it flow", "The catch unknown", "Small fish only", "Mind small ills"] },
    { no: 98, grade: "中平", title: "Guan Zhong and Bao Shuya Share Gold", titleZh: "管鲍分金", poem: "Planting jade in the hills - the field too narrow\nDigging for gold - annoyed by the crowd\nRich or poor is appointed above\nWhy must the world toil itself to the bone", poemZh: "入山种玉嫌田狭\n掘地寻金厌客多\n富贵贫穷天注定\n世人何苦力奔波", meaning: "Guan Zhong and Bao Shuya split their earnings, and Bao, knowing his friend's poverty, always gives the larger share - the friendship that became the proverb. Rich and poor are apportioned; do not run yourself ragged chasing coin, nor let profit bury duty. Keep money matters with friends clear and kind - the contented stay cheerful even poor. A harmonious home and an easy heart are the true wealth.", aspects: ["Honor before profit", "Content, be glad", "Share the gold", "Peace, good health"] },
    { no: 99, grade: "中平", title: "Han Yu Caught in the Snow", titleZh: "韩文公遇雪", poem: "Snow chokes the bridge-head; the horse will not advance\nWild wind - fisherman, do not set out\nThe stream flows, flowers fall - who cherishes them\nSet a firm heart early; let the aim not swerve", poemZh: "雪拥桥头马不前\n风狂渔父莫开船\n水流花谢人谁惜\n早立坚心志勿偏", meaning: "Han Yu, banished for his memorial, meets the snow-choked Lan Pass and cannot advance - season against him, road blocked. Fortune runs low and obstacles crowd, yet the poem's cure holds: fix the heart early, let nothing bend the aim. Do not lose heart in the strait; outlast the winter and clearing skies follow - though the household should mind its quarrels meanwhile.", aspects: ["Stand firm", "Hard, then easier", "Guard the base", "Mind the seasons"] },
    { no: 100, grade: "中吉", title: "Emperor Minghuang Admires the Flowers", titleZh: "唐明皇赏花", poem: "A hundred flowers race to open, hailing the warm spring\nAll things from this day turn new\nIn the last count, say not that fortune is spent\nUnnoticed, the worst has turned to best again", poemZh: "百花竞放贺阳春\n万物从今尽转新\n末数莫言穷运至\n不知否极泰来频", meaning: "A hundred blossoms salute the returning sun and everything turns new - the closing stick of the hundred, promising winter's end. The tide has bottomed and now turns: old patterns shed, forces gather, the last stretch anything but poor. Hold optimism and press forward; take the hand of the new turn, and the year closes with a full harvest. Whatever went before, the ending is renewal.", aspects: ["Tide has turned", "Renewed and rising", "Entering the good", "Vigor returns"] },
  ],
};
